0|0@nvidia^1440114736#cua3ejx:PrivateFluttershy$:DPFP.....No not in a serial computing environment which is dx11 nor pre vulkan open gl. DPFP only comes into play here because of Async Shaders = GFX and Compute running together. Async Shaders is one of the most basic of dx12 components. AMD GCN async shaders YES....pre maxwell 2 NO.....your gpu then has to preempt its tasks in serial like in dx11 which also leads to idling processors and further diminished performance. Which also explains the lack of gains and/or diminished performance compared to dx11. EDIT= Here this article should help clearify what I'm talking about. Graph of importance is toward the bottom [LINK](http://www.anandtech.com/show/9124/amd-dives-deep-on-asynchronous-shading)
